# Verification Plan — {{CAMPAIGN_TITLE}}

**How we will know a result is right — decided up front, before the work.** The campaign's tailored
verification gate: the application-specific checks and best-practices for *this* problem, captured at setup
(`new-campaign` / `frame-problem`) and kept living. `verify` reads this when adjudicating a finding;
`correctness-suite` encodes the checkable items and **promotes each hard-won one to a standing regression
gate**; `program.md`'s independent-verification step references it (the `{{VERIFY_EXTRA_CHECKS}}` hook).

> **Scope.** For a **simulation-heavy** campaign, the full V&V&UQ doctrine and its tailoring live in the
> campaign's `SIMULATION_VALIDATION.md`; this file then holds the *non-simulation* and *application-specific*
> checks. For a campaign with **no central simulation** (a fit on real data, a hardware loop), this file is
> the primary verification plan. Don't duplicate — point to whichever owns each check.

> **Living document.** Append new checks as the campaign uncovers them; when a bug is found, add the check
> that would have caught it (and promote it to a `correctness-suite` regression gate). Record the *why* of a
> non-obvious check in `ENGINEERING_NOTES.md`.

## A-priori expectations (the bound a result must respect)
- **Plausible range / order-of-magnitude** the primary result must fall within: {{APRIORI_RANGE}}
  *(a result outside this is a bug or a discovery — investigate before celebrating)*.
- **Hard physical bounds** (probabilities in [0,1], known ranges, conservation limits): {{HARD_BOUNDS}}.

## Verification checks — "are we computing it right?"
Mark each **V** (verification: solving the equations right). The checkable ones become regression gates.
- [ ] **Dimensional / units sanity** — run first (`dimensional-analysis`).
- [ ] **Analytic / closed-form limit** the result must reproduce: {{ANALYTIC_LIMITS}}.
- [ ] **Conservation / symmetry invariants** that must hold: {{INVARIANTS}}.
- [ ] **Numerical convergence** (if anything is discretized): {{CONVERGENCE_PLAN}}.
- [ ] **Independent-method parity** — a second, mechanism-diverse route that should agree: {{PARITY_METHOD}}.
- [ ] **Recompute every reported number** from a fresh run (no transcription); trivial/degenerate baselines beaten.

## Validation checks — "are we computing the right thing?"
Mark each **Val** (validation, on held-out / independent data — **calibration is not validation**).
- [ ] **Comparison to data / benchmark** with uncertainty on both sides: {{VALIDATION_DATA}}.
- [ ] **Validation hierarchy** (unit → subsystem → full system; watch compensating errors): {{VALIDATION_HIERARCHY}}.
- [ ] **Domain of applicability** stated; no silent extrapolation: {{DOMAIN}}.

## Application-specific checks & known gotchas (the field-standard part)
The checks "everyone in this subfield runs," known artifacts, and gotchas for *this* problem — the part
generic doctrine can't supply.
- [ ] {{APP_CHECK_1}}
- [ ] {{APP_CHECK_2}}
- **Known artifacts / failure modes to guard against:** {{KNOWN_ARTIFACTS}}.

## Residual / error interrogation
For any fit or prediction: examine **residuals for systematic structure** (trend, input-dependence,
spatial/temporal pattern, autocorrelation) vs random zero-mean noise — structure signals a bug or
unaccounted-for physics (a parked effect in the `PHYSICS.md` inventory), and is a discovery lead, not just
error to report. *(See `verify`.)*

## Promotion gate
A finding graduates to `DISCOVERIES.md` only when: the applicable checks above pass, it generalizes across
{{GENERALIZATION_AXIS}} (not a lucky subset), and an independent `verify` returns **CONFIRMED**.
